<title>BELGIUM: EU seeks 17 pct monthly sugar storage refund cut.</title>
<headline>EU seeks 17 pct monthly sugar storage refund cut.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission on Wednesday proposed to cut the 1997/98 monthly sugar storage refund by 17 percent to 0.35 Ecus per 100 kg.</p>
<p>Commission sources said the proposed reduction took account of lower interest rates.  </p>
<p>The Commission proposed, as part of the 1997/98 (July/June) farm price package, that the basic price for sugar beet remain at 47.67 Ecus a tonne.</p>
<p>The intervention price for white sugar would remain at 63.19 Ecus per 100 kg.</p>
<p>EU Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler will present on March 17-18 the farm price proposals to farm ministers, who are due to take a decision by end-June.</p>
<p>--Peter Blackburn, Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
